{
	"id": "doota",
	"name": "Doota",
	"repo": "ethercorps/doota",
	"url": "https://github.com/ethercorps/doota",
	"summary": "Doota is a self-hosted email app that runs on your own Cloudflare account: Email Routing delivers mail to Workers, which thread it into chat-style conversations stored encrypted in D1 and R2.",
	"description": "The D1 mail schema (mailboxes, aliases, threads, shared messages, per-mailbox deliveries and triage, attachments, labels, outbound submissions) and how an inbound email moves from the Email Routing Worker through the queue consumer into those tables.",
	"notes": "Tenant org_id FKs on message/delivery/thread_state/label/submission and secondary FKs (submission.fromAliasId/createdByUserId/apiKeyId, thread_label.mailboxId, delivery role 'from') are omitted to keep the diagram readable. Nullable-returning functions show the non-null type; union params use the first member; materializeDelivery's inline-object param is left untyped. The Worker class is the anonymous default export of apps/mail-in/src/index.ts, named after its wrangler name.",
